INT. DRIVE-THROUGH TAXIDERMY SHOP - DAY

A window with a menu board: "MOUNTS WHILE YOU WAIT." Behind it, shelves of glassy-eyed squirrels.

CLERK (19, headset, name tag hidden by a lanyard) leans out of the window. A CUSTOMER (60s, sunglasses, trucker cap) idles at the curb holding a shoebox.

CLERK
Welcome to Stuff It. What can I stuff for you?

CUSTOMER
My cat.

CLERK
Is he deceased?

CUSTOMER
She is. Hortense.

CLERK
Sorry for your loss. I'm Darnell.

Darnell takes the shoebox. Peeks inside. Winces.

DARNELL
Rigor?

HORTENSE
Three days.

A phone rings behind the counter. Darnell grabs it.

KEVIN (V.O.)
(over phone, shouting)
Darnell, did you tell the customer about the surcharge?

DARNELL
What surcharge?

KEVIN (V.O.)
The cat surcharge! Forty dollars!

Darnell holds the phone out the window. Hortense stares at it.

HORTENSE
Forty dollars to stuff my cat?

DARNELL
Per whisker.

HORTENSE
That's not funny.

DARNELL
No, ma'am. It's company policy.

A horn blares behind the truck.

IMPATIENT DRIVER (O.S.)
Hey! Some of us have raccoons waiting!

Hortense does not move. Neither does Darnell.
